    "earlyLife": "St. Cuthbert of Lindisfarne belongs to the history of Dunbar, Scotland during c. 634–687. Known for healing miracles and gift of prophecy. Hagiography preserves both documented events and pious memory; the Church canonizes saints when their holiness is clear, not when every anecdote is verified like a modern biography. Geography and era matter: knowing where this saint lived helps readers understand the political, religious, and economic pressures that shaped choices of courage, poverty, or exile.",
