    "historicalContext": "Parishes mark March 25 with proper readings, prayers, and often festive music when rubrics allow. Check your parish bulletin for Mass times; solemnities may include Gloria, Creed, and extended processions or blessings. In the United States, when this date is a Holy Day of Obligation, Catholics plan travel and work schedules around Mass — a countercultural witness in itself.",
