    "legacy": "Every generation re-encounters Nativity of the Blessed Virgin Mary on September 8 with new questions — suffering, hope, family fracture, or cultural hostility to faith. The feast answers by pointing to God's action, not human achievement. That is why calendar feasts remain among the most durable teachers in Catholic life: they return whether or not smartphones remind us.",
